WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:01.376
I don't really care what

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:03.170
anyone thinks I should be doing.

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.630
All I want to do is wrestle.

00:00:07.799 --> 00:00:09.635
When I first started
with the Monster Factory,

00:00:09.635 --> 00:00:10.761
I said to myself like if I

00:00:10.761 --> 00:00:13.263
got one person to the
WWE I'll be happy.

00:00:13.597 --> 00:00:14.890
Danny Cage,

00:00:14.932 --> 00:00:16.850
you have this school, 
the Monster Factory.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:17.935
He teaches you everything;

00:00:18.018 --> 00:00:19.061
how to do the cameras,

00:00:19.061 --> 00:00:20.187
be a referee,

00:00:20.187 --> 00:00:20.938
build a ring.

00:00:21.021 --> 00:00:23.023
Whenever we're doing
something in here,

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:24.566
you do it a hundred percent.

00:00:25.901 --> 00:00:28.403
I was working in one
of these dead end jobs.

00:00:28.445 --> 00:00:29.905
As soon as I walked in,
I was like...

00:00:29.905 --> 00:00:30.906
this is awesome.

00:00:32.574 --> 00:00:34.117
The rush of being
in a wrestling ring

00:00:34.117 --> 00:00:35.202
is like nothing else.

00:00:38.664 --> 00:00:39.706
Professional wrestling is,

00:00:39.790 --> 00:00:42.417
an eclectic melting
pot of misfits.

00:00:42.417 --> 00:00:43.210
I mean I'm from Philly.

00:00:43.210 --> 00:00:45.087
So, an underdog
is a hungry dog.

00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:47.047
Part of me didn't want to
call myself Twitch.

00:00:47.297 --> 00:00:49.132
But how many
wrestlers do you know

00:00:49.132 --> 00:00:51.260
not only have Tourette's
but are like open about it.

00:00:52.594 --> 00:00:53.887
Professional
wrestling is a very

00:00:53.887 --> 00:00:55.973
hard industry to make it in.

00:00:56.848 --> 00:00:57.933
The odds are against you.

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.352
I mean there's
thousands of wrestlers,

00:01:00.435 --> 00:01:02.938
everyday just trying
to get tryouts.

00:01:03.146 --> 00:01:05.565
But I've gotten
more people there 

00:01:05.607 --> 00:01:07.192
than any other
coach in the world.

00:01:07.568 --> 00:01:09.486
I could either walk
out as champion

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:11.947
or I could go back
to flipping burgers.

00:01:12.406 --> 00:01:13.573
We have forty students.

00:01:13.699 --> 00:01:14.950
They still have to get signed.

00:01:14.950 --> 00:01:16.076
They still have to get better.

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:16.827
Let's go.

00:01:16.868 --> 00:01:18.453
♪♪

00:01:18.453 --> 00:01:19.997
My body isn't what
it used to be.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.124
I saw this
goddess crumble.

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:24.918
You are good.
Right now you're not.

00:01:25.377 --> 00:01:26.586
It's just been an off night.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.879
There's a lot of
stuff happening.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.257
I tried to quit and
Dan didn't let me.

00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:33.051
I have just constant fear.

00:01:33.802 --> 00:01:35.679
Path to paradise
begins in hell

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:37.180
and if you're going
through hell,

00:01:37.681 --> 00:01:38.307
keep going.

00:01:38.307 --> 00:01:38.765
Go!

00:01:38.765 --> 00:01:42.060
♪♪

00:01:42.686 --> 00:01:43.353
Oh God!

00:01:43.395 --> 00:01:45.605
She got invited
for a WWE tryout.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.608
♪♪

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:53.113
♪♪

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:58.118
♪♪

00:02:00.871 --> 00:02:02.205
Wrestle for the WWE?

00:02:02.414 --> 00:02:03.832
Hell, that's the dream.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:06.918
Make sure they don't
kill each other.

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:09.421
Or if they do just clean up.

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:11.465
♪♪

